  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">NFiT projects for World Heritage 2023 Budget</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The NFiT aims to contribution to the &#x201C;Implementation of the World Heritage Convention&#x201D;.  
&#x2022;	support World Heritage Convention broadly including cultural, natural, and mixed heritage and also including all regions. 
&#x2022;	provide smaller &#x2018;seed funding&#x2019; for projects: the NFiT provides a useful means to support projects and reaches out to beneficiaries who otherwise would enable them to carry out the initial work necessary to attract further funding.
&#x2022;	support specific projects (heritage site and/or theme) in relation to key challenges facing world heritage over the coming years (for example, climate change, biodiversity, SIDS and sustainable development).
&#x2022;	support State Parties&apos; efforts to respond to the Decisions adopted by the World Heritage Committee to improve the State of Conservation of World Heritage properties. 
&#x2022;	support actions/activities identified during the Periodic Reporting exercise and in the regional World Heritage Action Plans.</narrative>
  </description>
